@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix ssn: <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/> .
@prefix desire: <http://example.org/agora/desire#> .
@prefix review: <http://example.org/agora/review#> .
@prefix perception: <http://example.org/agora/perception#> .
@prefix water: <http://example.org/agora/water#> .
@prefix reporting: <http://example.org/agora/reporting#> .
@prefix ag: <http://example.org/agora#> .
@prefix market: <http://example.org/agora/market#> .

#  Succulent's agent's PRIVATE beliefs. Note how far these diverge from fern's: it wants a
#  fifth of the moisture, shrugs at readings that would have fern bidding hard, and is
#  content to look rarely and to trust older data. Same world, same ontology, different mind.

##  perception:Subscribing
ag:succulent_agent
    perception:fastSleepS 60 ;
    perception:slowSleepS 900 ;
    perception:readingGraceS 45 .

##  market:Bidding
ag:succulent_agent
    market:hasEndowment 100.0 ;
    water:litresPerFraction 2.0 ;
    water:maxValuePerL 0.80 .

##  How often it says how it is — belief base size, reading freshness, silent write failures.
#   Omit this line and the agent reports nothing; see agora/metrics.py.
ag:succulent_agent reporting:metricsIntervalS 60 .

##  Self-review — how often at the very least.
#   Required because the world gave this agent room to move (review:commits, in world.ttl): an
#   agent granted none derives no review capability and needs no interval. A FLOOR and not a
#   schedule — a decision plans its own next arising from when its effect could show.
#   See knowledge/decisions/self-review-is-a-capability.md.
ag:succulent_agent review:reviewIntervalS 300 .

##  desire — the pick inside the region
#   The point this agent steers its moisture toward. PRIVATE where the region is public: the
#   region is deduced from what the plant states and answers to the sovereign; the aim answers
#   to the region (desire:AimShape) and to nobody else, which is what makes it this agent's.
#   It used to be water:hasTarget — one number that was also the market's pricing input. The
#   market now asks desire for it, so an agent in a world with no market could still hold one.
ag:succulent_agent desire:aims [ ssn:forProperty water:SoilMoisture ; schema:value 0.22 ] .
